[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Thus, we consider the divisors of \(9!\) that are coprime to 10. These divisors must be divisors of \(9! / (2^7 \times 5) = 3^4 \times 7\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m The prime factorization of \(3^4 \times 7\) is \(81 \times 7 = 567\). The divisors of 567 are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^0 \times 7^0 = 1\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^0 \times 7^1 = 7\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^1 \times 7^0 = 3\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^1 \times 7^1 = 21\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^2 \times 7^0 = 9\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^2 \times 7^1 = 63\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^3 \times 7^0 = 27\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^3 \times 7^1 = 189\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^4 \times 7^0 = 81\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m - \(3^4 \times 7^1 = 567\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m From these, the divisors of 567 that have a units digit of 1 are 1, 21, and 81. Summing these, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[1 + 21 + 81 = 103\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Thus, the sum of the positive divisors of \(9!\) that have units digit 1 is \(\boxed{103}\).
