[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m To find the sum of all integer bases \( b > 9 \) for which \( 17_b \) is a divisor of \( 97_b \), we start by converting the numbers from base \( b \) to decimal. The numbers are \( 17_b = b + 7 \) and \( 97_b = 9b + 7 \). We need \( b + 7 \) to divide \( 9b + 7 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m We set up the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Rearranging this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ (9 - k)b + (7 - 7k) = 0 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m We denote \( d = 9 - k \), so \( b = \frac{56}{d} - 7 \). We need \( b > 9 \), so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ \frac{56}{d} - 7 > 9 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ \frac{56}{d} > 16 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ d < 3.5 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m The divisors of 56 are considered, and we find that \( d \) must be a positive divisor of 56 and less than 3.5. The possible values are \( d = 1 \) and \( d = 2 \), giving \( b = 49 \) and \( b = 21 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
