[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Similarly, a=3,2^3=8.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 8*3^b*7^d≡1.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m This requires8*(3^b*7^d )≡1 ⇒3^b*7^d≡8^{-1}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m But inverse doesn’t exist as gcd(8,10)=2.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Thus, no solution.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Thus, in conclusion, the only such divisors are1 and21.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Therefore sum=1 +21=22.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
