[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m From the second equation, we express \( t \) as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ t = 2.4 - \frac{9}{s + 2} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Equating the two expressions for \( t \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 4 - \frac{9}{s} = 2.4 - \frac{9}{s + 2} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Simplifying:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 1.6 = \frac{18}{s(s + 2)} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 1.6 = \frac{18}{s(s + 2)} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 1.6s(s + 2) = 18 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 16s(s + 2) = 180 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 4s^2 + 8s - 45 = 0 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m Solving the quadratic equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ s = \frac{-8 \pm \sqrt{64 + 720}}{8} = \frac{-8 \pm 28}{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ s = 2.5 \text{ km/h} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
