[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m The prime factorization of \(9!\) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m \[ 9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5 \times 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=372176)[0m We need to find the divisors of \(9!\) that have a units digit of 1. These divisors must not be divisible by 5, so we consider the divisors of \(9! / 5 = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 7\).
